                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I just don't know what this crap is anymore.\n\nTime trial box shuffling puzzle stuff where you put out fires. Game starts, no tutorial, nothing. Can you figure out how to play it? Is probably the first puzzle. There is no menu, no settings, no controls. You just have to guess, I guess. For anyone wondering: it's space. Space let's you shoot water. Fair enough, space is an often used button. Still ... How do you move the blocks? Oh, you drag them. With the mouse. Okay.\n\nSo, now that that's settled, prepare for the \"gameplay\". Move boxes to create lanes to put out fires. Rinse, repeat. Literally. Then, learn the level by heart, figure out how to efficiently move each block, WRITE IT DOWN, then do the level again if you want to even have a glimmer of hope of beating the par time. Do you need to beat that par time? Who knows. I played through the first 10 levels, there are 15 more. Are there more after that? Do you need to beat a certain amount of levels \"on par\" to unlock more? I don't know ... and I don't want to know.\n\nYou cannot even move blocks AND shoot water at the same time.\n\nThis is garbage and clearly designed for phones.",
